// Chapter 14: Shared C Runtime & AOT Compilation

Heading { id -> `sec-runtime`, text -> `Shared C Runtime & AOT Compilation`, size -> 1 },

Paragraph {
    text -> `Zenlang achieves high performance and cross-platform portability by sharing a unified C runtime (runtime/) between interpreted scripts and Ahead-Of-Time (-g) compiled native binaries. Both execution paths share the same ZenValue ABI, enabling compiled modules to seamlessly interoperate with interpreted scripts.`
},

Diagram {
    type -> `flow`,
    direction -> `right`,
    nodes -> [`Zen AST / Bytecode`, `C Transpiler`, `Clang / GCC`, `Native Binary`]
},

Callout {
    type -> `important`,
    title -> `Unified ZenValue ABI`,
    text -> `Interpreted scripts can import and call pre-compiled C modules without wrapper glue code or foreign-function overhead because both layers utilize identical ZenValue struct layouts.`
},

Table {
    headers -> [`Execution Mode`, `Compiler Command`, `Target Environment`, `Primary Advantage`],
    rows -> [
        [`Interpreted VM`, `zen script.zl`, `Development & Scripting`, `Instant zero-compile startup & dynamic reload`],
